Third-party material
--------------------

- solidcore (https://github.com/tangency-labs/solidcore), Apache-2.0: the B-rep kernel, used as a
  dependency (crates solidcore, solidcore-ops, solidcore-record, solidcore-convert, solidcore-tess,
  step-brep, step-export), pinned by git revision. Only crates/kernel depends on it.

- SolidCraft (https://github.com/tangency-labs/solidcraft), MIT OR Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) 2026 SolidCraft
  contributors: the STEP open-shell writer in crates/io/src/step/ is adapted from its crates/step, and
  the IGES writer crates/io/src/iges.rs from its crates/kernel/src/iges_out.rs (both modified).

- Instant Meshes (https://github.com/wjakob/instant-meshes; permissive licence, see its LICENSE.txt: design doc §10
  records it as MIT, the repository file reads BSD-3-Clause; re-check before any source is adapted), Copyright (c)
  2015 Wenzel Jakob, Daniele Panozzo, Marco Tarini and Olga Sorkine-Hornung ("Instant Field-Aligned Meshes",
  SIGGRAPH Asia 2015): the retopology in crates/fit/src/retopo.rs implements the orientation and position field
  method of that paper, written from the publication; no source code of the reference implementation was copied
  or adapted.

Adapted source files are listed in ATTRIBUTION.md ("Adapted code"), each keeping its original
copyright notice and marked as modified (Apache-2.0 section 4).

SurfaceCraft contains no code, icons, text or data from QuickSurface or Geomagic Design X; their
documented behaviour was studied only as a functional reference (clean-room).
